From: Alan Shearer
Subject: udp: enqueue the incoming buffer on unicast instead of cloning

Unicast demux has one matching endpoint. StoreData always EnqueueClone()s
the already-deframed datagram; ReceiveData then frees the original. That
is a full net_buffer clone on every localhost / unicast packet (iperf3
-u against 127.0.0.1).

Enqueue the incoming buffer itself and transfer ownership. Broadcast and
DeliverData still clone: they can fan out to more than one socket.

If the socket FIFO is full, Enqueue does not take the buffer; free it
in _DemuxUnicast so ReceiveData does not double-free on the success path.

Ticket: https://dev.haiku-os.org/ticket/18730

---

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/network/protocols/udp/udp.cpp
@@ -626,7 +626,15 @@
 		return B_NAME_NOT_FOUND;
 	}
 
-	endpoint->StoreData(buffer);
+	// Unicast has a single recipient. Hand the already-deframed buffer
+	// to the socket queue instead of cloning it. Enqueue takes ownership
+	// only on success.
+	status_t status = endpoint->Enqueue(buffer);
+	if (status != B_OK) {
+		gBufferModule->free(buffer);
+		return B_OK;
+	}
+
 	return B_OK;
 }
 
 
@@ -762,8 +770,13 @@
 		return B_ERROR;
 	}
 
-	gBufferModule->free(buffer);
-	return B_OK;
+	// Broadcast still clones inside StoreData; free the original here.
+	// Unicast Enqueue already took (or freed) the buffer in _DemuxUnicast.
+	if ((buffer->msg_flags & MSG_BCAST) != 0)
+		gBufferModule->free(buffer);
+
+	return B_OK;
 }
 
 
